{
  "description": "A Collie Client's hello accepted, then the `finish-stop-and-progress` client conformance case (ADRs 0029 and 0102): the Run `nightly` answers its progress at once, its program sets its progress message, and the next read, sent with the last value's position as `after`, answers the value carrying it; its finish with a timeout of 60 s fails with `deadline_exceeded`, which ends only the wait, and its next finish answers the whole Run report. The Run `weekly`'s stop answers it stopped as an abort by its program, with its Checkpoint. The Run `broken` ended `failed`, so its finish and its stop fail with the error that failed it, and the Connection's close aborts it, answered its report; the Client then closes.",
